  "id": "rhbi-v3",
  "mechanism_class": "structural",
  "mechanism_rationale": "In rhbi-v2, stateful batch-bound critic view wrappers on trajectory and residual_student failed concatenation inside RHBICriticPenalty, while 1-to-1 joint OT across distinct continuous condition draws (c_i != c_j on DDGAN reverse steps and continuous-context student hosts) acted as singleton-fibre squared-error regression toward the conditional mean E[x_0 | c_i] and mixed unnormalized condition baselines b(c_i) across batch rows. Setting rhbi_conditional_fibre='slack' cancels per-fibre baselines b(c_i) identically on continuous-conditioned fibres without altering critic penalty calibration or unconditional/discrete-conditional Sinkhorn transport, while stateful-view detection in RHBICriticPenalty restores clean endpoint Lipschitz regularization on batch-bound closures.",
